# Introduction to FortiAIOps
## Hands-on Lab Guide v1.1

!!! info "Lab Overview"
    This hands-on lab provides comprehensive experience with FortiAIOps v3.0.0, covering initial setup, device integration, monitoring capabilities, and AI-powered insights across the Fortinet Security Fabric.

---

## Lab Objectives

The FortiAIOps vision is to provide real-time insights and visibility across the entire Fortinet Fabric, rather than just the edge or wireless network, with the ultimate goal of improving the user experience.

This lab aims to:

- **Familiarize** you with FortiAIOps provisioning processes
- **Demonstrate** key features and functions through hands-on experience
- **Provide** knowledge needed for proof of concepts and demonstrations
- **Ensure** proper configuration for comprehensive data collection

---

## Lab Topology

<div class="grid cards" markdown>

-   :material-router-wireless:{ .lg .middle } **FortiPoC Instances**

    ---

    25x FortiPoC instances (PoC-01 through PoC-25)

    Access via: `https://10.222.14.XX` (where XX is your pod number)

-   :material-security-network:{ .lg .middle } **Security Fabric**

    ---

    Complete Fortinet ecosystem deployment with integrated monitoring

    Real-time insights across all fabric components

</div>

### Components Per FortiPoC Instance

| Component | Type | Description |
|-----------|------|-------------|
| **FGT-WAN** | FortiGate-VM | Internet access and core routing |
| **FGT-WLC** | FortiGate-VM | Wireless LAN Controller with FortiLink |
| **FortiSwitch** | 224E-POE | Physical switch with 4 connected APs |
| **FortiAPs** | 2x FAP-231F, 2x FAP-231G | Connected to FSW ports 1-4 |
| **FortiAIOps** | VM | AI Operations and monitoring platform |
| **Client Devices** | Windows 10/11 | Testing endpoints |

