## Authorize the FortiSwitch on FGT-WLC

On your lab FortiGate, FGT-WLC, within the HTTPS web GUI, perform the
following;

-   Navigate to **Wi-Fi & Switch Controller \> Managed FortiSwitches**

```{=html}
<!-- -->
```
-   **Select** and **Authorize** the listed FortiSwitch so that your
    FortiGate can manage it

![](media/image16.png){width="6.489583333333333in"
height="2.9895833333333335in"}

If you don't see your FortiSwitch listed or it's not coming online this
is likely because the FortiLink physical interface stays online during
the lab reset process, resulting in the switch not sending out a
discovery packet (a side effect of virtualisation) you will need to
bounce (disable/enable) the FortiLink interface in order for your
FortiGate to detect the FortiSwitch connected to it. To do this;

-   Within the FortiOS GUI navigate to **WiFi & Switch Controller \>
    FortiLink Interface**

-   Under Status at the bottom of this window select the **Disable**
    option then select the **Apply** button

-   Again under status select the **Enable** option then select the
    **Apply** button.

-   Navigate to **WiFi & Switch Controller \> Managed FortiSwitches**
    and confirm your **FortiSwitch is now**

-   ![](media/image17.png){width="5.626388888888889in"
    height="1.5666666666666667in"}The FortiSwitch will take **up to 2-3
    minutes to come online**, as per the image below. In the meantime,
    please continue with the lab; there should be no need to wait for
    this. If it doesn't come online after this amount of time, please
    advise the team provisioning this HOL.

### 1.4 Create VLANs

#### AP Management VLAN

![](media/image18.png){width="2.0375in" height="2.120833333333333in"}

Navigate to **WiFi & Switch Controller → FortiSwitch VLANs** → **Create New**

```yaml
Name: AP-Mgmt
VLAN: 10
Color: Light Blue
Addressing Mode: Manual
IP: 192.168.10.1/24
Administrative Access:
  - Ping: Enabled
  - Security Fabric Connection: Enabled
  - DHCP Server: Enabled
DHCP Settings:
  - DNS Server: Same as Interface IP
  - NTP Server: Local
  - Wireless Controllers: Same as Interface IP
```

![](media/image19.png){width="3.1993055555555556in" height="3.325in"}

![](media/image20.png){width="3.06875in" height="2.975in"}

#### Client VLAN-A

![](media/image21.png){width="3.4291666666666667in" height="3.433333333333333in"}

```yaml
Name: Client-VLAN-A
VLAN: 20
Color: Orange
Addressing Mode: Manual
IP: 192.168.20.1/24
Administrative Access:
  - Ping: Enabled
  - DHCP Server: Enabled
DHCP Settings:
  - Address Range: 192.168.20.2-192.168.20.254
  - DNS Server: Same as Interface IP
  - NTP Server: Local
```

![](media/image22.png){width="3.2222222222222223in" height="3.886770559930009in"}

#### Client VLAN-B

![](media/image23.png){width="3.683333333333333in" height="3.683333333333333in"}

```yaml
Name: Client-VLAN-B
VLAN: 30
Color: Purple
Addressing Mode: Manual
IP: 192.168.30.1/24
Administrative Access:
  - Ping: Enabled
  - DHCP Server: Enabled
DHCP Settings:
  - DNS Server: Same as Interface IP
  - NTP Server: Local
```

![](media/image24.png){width="3.3368055555555554in" height="3.6666666666666665in"}

-   Select the **OK** button

