## Inventory Dashboard

As per Section 7, this is where you can add, remove, or reboot
FortiGates from within FortiAIOps. However, it's also where you need to
go to access the Diagnostics and Tools for any FortiGate monitored by
FortiAIOps.

Within the FortiAIOps GUI

-   Navigate to **Inventory \> Managed FortiGates**

-   Select your lab FGT-WLC, and then select the View Details button
    from the menu bar above it

![](media/image141.png){width="6.490972222222222in"
height="1.6111111111111112in"}

The Diagnostics and Tools slide-out/pop-up window should appear

Within the Diagnostics and Tools section, a significant amount of data
is made available at a per-FortiGate level. At a high level;

-   You can look at the performance over time

-   Wireless Channel Summary for any managed APs

-   Check the status of any managed FortiAPs, FortiSwitch, and connected
    clients, as well as the ability to drill down into each of these.

-   Full event log history

-   And Tools...

There are many tools available within FortiAIOps that can save a
significant amount of time and simplify troubleshooting or even logging
a TAC case.

You'll notice that from within FortiAIOps, you can run;

-   A Packet Capture

-   Check the ARP table

-   Check the Routing Table

-   Check DHCP addresses that have been leased

-   Perform DNS and Reverse DNS queries

-   Access the FortiGate CLI

-   Check the processes running

-   Run a TAC report

### What's a TAC report?

It's a report that should be included with every FortiCare ticket logged
where a FortiGate, Managed FortiAP, and/or managed FortiSwitch is
involved.

Included within this report are a number of status and diagnostics
commands that TAC would typically need to assist with diagnosing an
issue. By including this report upfront, it will reduce the time to
resolution, as TAC will be given a substantial amount of information to
start with, rather than needing to go back and forth asking for the
output of specific CLI commands.

-   Within the Diagnostics and Tools \> Tools window, select the **Run**
    button next to the **TAC Report** option

![](media/image142.png){width="6.5in"
height="3.1166666666666667in"}

This should trigger the TAC Report to be downloaded from within
FortiAIOs.

-   Save and open the TAC Report to view the level of information
    included

![](media/image143.png){width="5.392133639545057in"
height="2.1335181539807526in"}

